otic systems</article-title><source>Phys Rep</source><year>2002</year><volume>366</volume><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>101</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="R101"><label>101</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hadjipapas</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Hillebrand</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Holliday</surname><given-names>IE</given-names></name><name><surname>Singh</surname><given-names>KD</given-names></name><name><surname>Barnes</surname><given-names>GR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Assessing interactions of linear and nonlinear neuronal sources using MEG beamformers: a proof of concept</article-title><source>Clin Neurophysiol</source><year>2005</year><volume>116</volume><fpage>1300</fpage><lpage>13</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15978493</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="R102"><label>102</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bak</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Tang</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Wiesenfeld</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Self-organized criticality: An explanation of 1/f noise</article-title><source>Phys Rev Lett</source><year>1987</year><volume>59</volume><fpage>364</fpage><lpage>74</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="R103"><label>103</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Szentagothai</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The neuron network of the cerebral cortex: a functional interpretation</article-title><source>Proc R Soc Lond B Biol Sci</source><year>1978</year><volume>201</volume><fpage>219</fpage><lpage>48</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">27801</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="R104"><label>104</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-typ